is it the dragon no luster grizzlies at two o'clock it's a whole pack they're kicking up the snow

3
00:00:43,420 --> 00:00:51,840
how many eight no ten they know we're here and they're headed straight for us get ready

4
00:00:51,840 --> 00:01:00,120
run out guys quagmire get down here we need you yes sir quagmire yep

5
00:01:00,120 --> 00:01:05,680
charge

6
00:01:05,680 --> 00:01:12,680
run out

7
00:01:14,100 --> 00:01:17,060
yeah

8
00:01:18,300 --> 00:01:24,300
you

9
00:01:31,300 --> 00:01:33,300
Oh

10
00:01:35,680 --> 00:01:42,680
Hey! It's the Red Dragon! Look out!

11
00:01:42,680 --> 00:01:45,680
That's where the bears were running from!

12
00:01:55,680 --> 00:01:58,680
Hey Quagmire, what the hell is this?

13
00:01:58,680 --> 00:02:00,680
You better not have been slacking off!

14
00:02:00,680 --> 00:02:02,680
I couldn't see it through that cloud of snow!

15
00:02:05,680 --> 00:02:11,680
Damn it! Retreat! Now!

16
00:02:14,680 --> 00:02:17,680
We'll conjure a smokescreen! Everyone split up!

17
00:02:35,680 --> 00:02:53,680
Up.

18
00:02:53,680 --> 00:02:55,680
Renden.

19
00:02:55,680 --> 00:03:09,860
He got it!

20
00:03:09,860 --> 00:03:11,660
He got it!

21
00:03:14,660 --> 00:03:16,220
Nice going.

22
00:03:25,680 --> 00:03:30,720
You really are something special, Quagmire, you know that?

23
00:03:30,840 --> 00:03:33,420
You weren't kidding about traveling the Demon Continent, huh?

24
00:03:33,700 --> 00:03:36,460
Yeah, for real. I can't believe you actually beat that thing.

25
00:03:37,080 --> 00:03:38,900
Well, it was pretty weak already.

26
00:03:39,260 --> 00:03:43,840
Say, Quagmire, don't you think it's about damn time you joined our party for real?

27
00:03:44,400 --> 00:03:47,880
You fit right in, and I know you don't mind our company too terribly.

28
00:03:48,080 --> 00:03:51,980
Yeah, but once I make a name for myself out here, I'll have to move on again.

29
00:03:52,380 --> 00:03:54,460
Sorry, but I still need to find my mother.

30
00:03:55,680 --> 00:04:07,840
Thank you for protecting me out there today.

31
00:04:25,680 --> 00:04:43,680
And then it appeared...

32
00:04:43,680 --> 00:04:46,700
A giant red dragon!

33
00:04:48,760 --> 00:04:51,460
But when it seemed as though all hope was lost,

34
00:04:51,620 --> 00:04:55,160
he ensnared the great beast inside his namesake, a Quagmire,

35
00:04:55,840 --> 00:04:58,760
and dropped a massive boulder on the struggling worm!

36
00:04:59,320 --> 00:05:00,620
Tell a different one!

37
00:05:02,260 --> 00:05:03,760
That's not very nice.

38
00:05:04,120 --> 00:05:06,400
The hero of the story is sitting right here.

39
00:05:06,400 --> 00:05:20,440
I finally found you, Quagmire Rudeus.

40
00:05:20,520 --> 00:05:21,020
Uh...

41
00:05:21,020 --> 00:05:22,260
Shit.

42
00:05:22,740 --> 00:05:24,140
We're sitting right there.

43
00:05:24,140 --> 00:05:26,760
Yes, ma'am.

44
00:05:26,800 --> 00:05:28,200
You've tracked me down at last.

45
00:05:28,560 --> 00:05:30,960
I have no idea who this lady is.

46
00:05:31,360 --> 00:05:34,720
Yeah, you stick out like a sore thumb, just like she said you would.

47
00:05:34,720 --> 00:05:37,420
I haven't been trying to hide.

48
00:05:37,940 --> 00:05:40,680
Yes, well, I assumed you would be further out east.

49
00:05:45,880 --> 00:05:47,080
What is this?

50
00:05:47,460 --> 00:05:48,420
Love at first sight?

51
00:05:49,020 --> 00:05:50,780
Or is she just after my body?

52
00:05:51,140 --> 00:05:53,000
I have gotten manlier lately.

53
00:05:53,520 --> 00:05:55,420
Plenty of muscle these days, etc.

54
00:05:55,800 --> 00:05:57,760
I'm still a growing boy after all.

55
00:05:58,160 --> 00:05:58,760
What's wrong?

56
00:05:58,760 --> 00:06:00,180
Oh, nothing.

57
00:06:00,620 --> 00:06:01,440
Nothing at all.

58
00:06:02,520 --> 00:06:04,340
Who knew Quagmire had a woman?

59
00:06:06,120 --> 00:06:06,480
Hmm.

60
00:06:12,320 --> 00:06:14,660
My name is Alina Lise Dragon Road.

61
00:06:15,020 --> 00:06:17,500
You may know this, but in case you don't,

62
00:06:17,760 --> 00:06:20,920
I used to be in the same adventuring party as your father, Paul.

63
00:06:21,160 --> 00:06:21,640
Oh, yeah?

64
00:06:22,000 --> 00:06:22,620
Yes, indeed.

65
00:06:23,040 --> 00:06:24,720
I'm also a friend of Roxy's.

66
00:06:25,040 --> 00:06:25,520
Really?

67
00:06:25,880 --> 00:06:26,840
You know my master?

68
00:06:27,400 --> 00:06:28,680
Where is she these days?

69
00:06:29,180 --> 00:06:30,060
That can wait.

70
00:06:31,560 --> 00:06:32,920
Let's talk about you.

71
00:06:33,220 --> 00:06:35,940
I heard you brought down a red worm all by yourself.

72
00:06:37,380 --> 00:06:40,060
Yes, although it was half dead already.

73
00:06:40,940 --> 00:06:43,540
I can see why Roxy boasts about you.

74
00:06:44,600 --> 00:06:45,420
Does she really?

75
00:06:45,560 --> 00:06:48,040
That's very flattering to hear, if a little embarrassed.

76
00:06:48,300 --> 00:06:49,340
And you're touching me.

77
00:06:49,500 --> 00:06:51,000
You don't mind, do you?

78
00:06:51,260 --> 00:06:52,660
My, how strong you are.

79
00:06:52,780 --> 00:06:54,300
Sorry, I'm kind of confused.

80
00:06:54,300 --> 00:06:56,860
Do you have a thing for me by any chance?

81
00:06:57,100 --> 00:06:58,180
Oh, yes.

82
00:06:58,180 --> 00:06:59,500
You're so muscular.

83
00:06:59,920 --> 00:07:01,140
Exactly my type.

84
00:07:01,380 --> 00:07:02,640
You're a real man.

85
00:07:02,880 --> 00:07:05,240
I had expected you would be more of a child still.

86
00:07:07,140 --> 00:07:07,740
Okay.

87
00:07:08,900 --> 00:07:11,760
Well, you're quite lovely yourself, Miss Selina Lise.

88
00:07:12,240 --> 00:07:12,640
Ha!

89
00:07:13,060 --> 00:07:14,860
Her teasing won't fluster me.

90
00:07:14,860 --> 00:07:16,180
I'm not some virgin.

91
00:07:16,180 --> 00:07:16,200
I'm not some virgin.

92
00:07:20,200 --> 00:07:21,960
Whoa, wait.

93
00:07:22,660 --> 00:07:24,860
She's putting out some serious vibes here.

94
00:07:25,420 --> 00:07:27,080
Uh, you know what?

95
00:07:27,460 --> 00:07:28,920
Okay, let's do this thing.

96
00:07:28,920 --> 00:07:31,340
Oh, my goodness.

97
00:07:32,040 --> 00:07:33,820
However, did you come by this pendant?

98
00:07:34,420 --> 00:07:35,800
It's rough, but it's charming.

99
00:07:36,480 --> 00:07:38,780
Oh, that was a gift from a friend.

100
00:07:39,380 --> 00:07:40,160
A friend?

101
00:07:40,680 --> 00:07:41,740
Were they elvish?

102
00:07:42,460 --> 00:07:42,640
Huh?

103
00:07:43,300 --> 00:07:44,120
Uh, yeah.

104
00:07:44,480 --> 00:07:45,140
She is.

105
00:07:45,660 --> 00:07:47,300
Uh, why do you ask?

106
00:07:47,940 --> 00:07:49,600
No, there goes my shot.

107
00:07:49,600 --> 00:07:50,780
No real reason.

108
00:07:50,980 --> 00:07:51,640
Just curious.

109
00:07:52,920 --> 00:07:54,120
Here, look at this.

110
00:07:55,860 --> 00:07:56,820
We match.

111
00:07:58,080 --> 00:07:59,280
I guess we do.

112
00:07:59,540 --> 00:08:00,740
But I forget myself.

113
00:08:01,140 --> 00:08:02,520
Do excuse the come on.

114
00:08:02,520 --> 00:08:05,280
I wish you wouldn't tease me like that.

115
00:08:05,520 --> 00:08:06,360
Oh, dear boy.

116
00:08:06,560 --> 00:08:08,640
If there's one thing I never do, it's tease.

117
00:08:08,880 --> 00:08:12,480
But I have no intention of becoming Paul's daughter-in-law by any means.

118
00:08:12,640 --> 00:08:15,080
And I would prefer to remain friends with Roxy.

119
00:08:17,040 --> 00:08:20,360
So, I take it you have some business here with me, then?

120
00:08:22,000 --> 00:08:22,440
Yes.

121
00:08:22,980 --> 00:08:25,200
I've come to bring you a bit of good news.

122
00:08:26,840 --> 00:08:27,660
Have you now?

123
00:08:32,520 --> 00:08:36,640
That day, I learned where Zenith was.

124
00:08:37,320 --> 00:08:41,180
The labyrinth city of Rapa on the Begarit continent, far to the south.

125
00:08:41,700 --> 00:08:43,220
The other side of the world.

126
00:08:44,540 --> 00:08:49,000
Traveling there on foot from the northern territories could take a year, maybe more.

127
00:08:50,920 --> 00:08:53,660
Besides, winter is coming.

128
00:08:56,400 --> 00:09:00,400
I'll have to stay put for the time being, but I shouldn't have anything to worry about.

129
00:09:00,400 --> 00:09:04,960
According to Alina Lee, Zenith is having a grand old time going dungeon diving.

130
00:09:06,960 --> 00:09:07,400
And...

131
00:09:07,400 --> 00:09:10,700
Don't fall over yourself to leave just yet.

132
00:09:11,120 --> 00:09:15,280
We met Roxy while searching for your family and only split up once we found where Zenith was.

133
00:09:15,680 --> 00:09:20,780
She and the others should have joined up with Paul in Militian by now and made their way down to Begarit to get her.

134
00:09:21,200 --> 00:09:22,540
So you can relax, okay?

135
00:09:23,000 --> 00:09:23,940
Wait, go back.

136
00:09:24,140 --> 00:09:26,860
My master has been part of the search party all this time?

137
00:09:26,860 --> 00:09:32,000
Paul doesn't inspire much confidence, but if Roxy's there, good.

138
00:09:32,000 --> 00:09:42,820
Oh, Ridaeus.

139
00:09:43,260 --> 00:09:44,300
Welcome back.

140
00:09:45,300 --> 00:09:46,200
Morning, Alina Lee.

141
00:09:46,860 --> 00:09:48,600
See, you're active, bright and early.

142
00:09:49,580 --> 00:09:49,940
Active?

143
00:09:50,420 --> 00:09:50,660
I...

144
00:09:50,660 --> 00:09:52,900
Sure, I don't know what you mean by that.

145
00:09:52,900 --> 00:09:57,320
It is pretty cold today, though, so try not to catch a chill.

146
00:09:58,060 --> 00:10:03,000
Over the past week, I've learned that Alina Lee is slutty as hell, like damn.

147
00:10:03,760 --> 00:10:06,440
She's got a different man in her room almost every day.

148
00:10:07,000 --> 00:10:07,760
Sometimes two.

149
00:10:08,060 --> 00:10:08,700
Or three.

150
00:10:08,700 --> 00:10:18,060
The woman is a total man-eater.

151
00:10:18,680 --> 00:10:20,840
Not that I'm judging her for it, of course.

152
00:10:21,320 --> 00:10:25,720
I'd love to participate myself, but that's just not gonna happen.

153
00:10:26,480 --> 00:10:31,160
Because for two years now, I've been suffering from a certain sickness.

154
00:10:32,240 --> 00:10:35,160
The sickness of both body and mind.

155
00:10:35,160 --> 00:10:42,780
In short, it's E.D.

156
00:10:43,820 --> 00:10:44,720
And I've given up.

157
00:10:45,240 --> 00:10:48,880
At a certain point, I realize no one can help me fix this.

158
00:10:50,460 --> 00:10:53,020
And I don't like anyone enough to keep trying.

159
00:10:53,800 --> 00:10:56,180
If all my attempts at romance are gonna end in betrayal,

160
00:10:57,020 --> 00:10:59,420
I'd rather just admire from afar.

161
00:10:59,420 --> 00:11:04,640
I swear I'm not crying.

162
00:11:11,000 --> 00:11:15,080
Hey, this isn't what it looks like, Quagmire.

163
00:11:15,280 --> 00:11:17,720
I had no intention of putting my hands on your woman.

164
00:11:18,420 --> 00:11:19,360
Relax, soul.

165
00:11:19,500 --> 00:11:20,160
It's all right.

166
00:11:20,380 --> 00:11:23,240
Alina Lee isn't and has never been my woman.

167
00:11:24,020 --> 00:11:27,000
Besides, you know I'm not exactly in working order.

168
00:11:27,000 --> 00:11:29,380
Oh, yeah, right, I forgot.

169
00:11:30,020 --> 00:11:33,200
Sorry about that, didn't mean to go rubbing salt in the wound there or anything.

170
00:11:33,760 --> 00:11:34,880
I know, you're fine.

171
00:11:35,340 --> 00:11:36,020
But it was good?

172
00:11:36,260 --> 00:11:37,160
You had fun, right?

173
00:11:37,480 --> 00:11:37,980
Oh, yeah.

174
00:11:38,420 --> 00:11:39,360
She was amazing.

175
00:11:40,840 --> 00:11:43,880
Well, you heard the man Alina Lee's rave reviews.

176
00:11:44,500 --> 00:11:45,980
I know, it's what I do.

177
00:11:46,520 --> 00:11:49,760
I'm proud to say I've never had a man who's left unsatisfied.

178
00:11:50,580 --> 00:11:50,980
Really?

179
00:11:51,220 --> 00:11:51,860
Good for them.

180
00:11:51,860 --> 00:11:59,160
A few of the other guys in Soul's party have said the same to me already, but I'm not entirely sure they think of her as a team effort.

181
00:12:00,100 --> 00:12:01,140
Just do me a favor.

182
00:12:01,780 --> 00:12:02,260
Anything.

183
00:12:03,180 --> 00:12:07,940
You're obviously free to help yourself to whomever, but deal with the aftermath on your own.

184
00:12:08,360 --> 00:12:09,260
Oh, naturally.

185
00:12:09,860 --> 00:12:10,340
Sorry.

186
00:12:10,700 --> 00:12:11,800
What are you talking about?

187
00:12:11,880 --> 00:12:12,280
Nothing.

188
00:12:12,500 --> 00:12:13,280
Don't you worry.

189
00:12:14,120 --> 00:12:16,300
Now why don't we get something to eat?

190
00:12:16,300 --> 00:12:18,360
She's shameless.

191
00:12:19,420 --> 00:12:24,360
But she crossed the Demon Continent with Roxy and then made her way here alone, all for Paul's sake.

192
00:12:24,760 --> 00:12:27,180
So, she's gotta be a hell of a warrior.

193
00:12:27,960 --> 00:12:29,100
With Roxy.

194
00:12:29,640 --> 00:12:30,660
That'd be nice.

195
00:12:32,160 --> 00:12:34,480
Damn you two, can't a guy eat in peace?

196
00:12:35,360 --> 00:12:40,820
Super not jealous or anything, but how does this woman keep a harem of dudes around her and still avoid drama?

197
00:12:40,820 --> 00:12:45,820
I mean, as long as the fallout doesn't hit me, whatever, but...

198
00:12:45,820 --> 00:12:46,960
Here you are.

199
00:12:47,180 --> 00:12:48,860
The money I promised you.

200
00:12:49,680 --> 00:12:50,880
Thank you, m'lady.

201
00:12:51,360 --> 00:12:54,820
You know, I feel kind of bad getting paid for something that felt that good.

202
00:12:55,260 --> 00:12:56,340
Well, stop that.

203
00:12:56,780 --> 00:12:59,180
Just don't get serious about me and we're fine.

204
00:12:59,740 --> 00:13:03,740
Oh, so this is kind of a reverse prostitution thing.

205
00:13:04,400 --> 00:13:05,620
I guess that's okay.

206
00:13:06,200 --> 00:13:06,700
Right?

207
00:13:06,700 --> 00:13:25,580
Don't mind me, just delivering your mail.

208
00:13:26,440 --> 00:13:27,780
Oh, thank you.

209
00:13:32,120 --> 00:13:36,380
To Lord Rudeus Greyrat, I hope this letter finds you well.

210
00:13:36,700 --> 00:13:41,160
I am Genus Vice-Principal of the Rinoa University of Magic.

211
00:13:42,120 --> 00:13:43,300
Wait a sec, holy crap!

212
00:13:43,700 --> 00:13:44,880
That's Roxy's alma mater!

213
00:13:46,260 --> 00:13:50,760
Word of your exploits is Quagmire Rudeus has reached us here in the Kingdom of Rinoa.

214
00:13:51,380 --> 00:13:54,340
I understand you can cast spells without incantations,

215
00:13:54,780 --> 00:14:00,080
and I've been informed that you also studied under Roxy Magurdia, a King-class Water Mage.

216
00:14:00,080 --> 00:14:04,880
Should you have any desire to hone your magnificent craft further still,

217
00:14:05,200 --> 00:14:09,580
Rinoa University of Magic would be honored to welcome you as a special student.

218
00:14:09,860 --> 00:14:10,200
Ooh!

219
00:14:11,840 --> 00:14:13,100
Sounds important.

220
00:14:13,960 --> 00:14:17,720
Special students are exempt from both tuition and regular class attendance,

221
00:14:18,060 --> 00:14:21,860
but retain full access to our on-campus libraries and other facilities

222
00:14:21,860 --> 00:14:24,320
to conduct their own research as they see fit.

223
00:14:24,980 --> 00:14:25,540
Wow!

224
00:14:25,900 --> 00:14:27,160
Sounds like a good deal.

225
00:14:30,400 --> 00:14:32,320
Would love to meet with you.

226
00:14:32,560 --> 00:14:34,580
Thank you for your time and consideration.

227
00:14:35,260 --> 00:14:37,600
Signed God knows who from God knows where.

228
00:14:37,600 --> 00:14:41,440
I am glad someone appreciates my two years of hard work,

229
00:14:41,640 --> 00:14:45,760
and it's true that my magic's kind of plateaued, so I am interested.

230
00:14:46,500 --> 00:14:49,620
But I need to verify the authenticity of this thing.

231
00:14:52,120 --> 00:14:53,140
Thank you for waiting.

232
00:14:54,060 --> 00:14:57,140
Oh, that special student program. Good stuff.

233
00:14:57,540 --> 00:14:58,540
So you do know it.

234
00:14:58,760 --> 00:15:01,200
Yeah, I thought I'd heard that you attended school there.

235
00:15:01,680 --> 00:15:03,440
Can you tell me anything more about it?

236
00:15:04,000 --> 00:15:05,360
Well, I didn't graduate.

237
00:15:05,360 --> 00:15:07,140
I dropped out in my fifth year.

238
00:15:07,600 --> 00:15:11,080
But yeah, the university will sometimes reach out to people like you,

239
00:15:11,220 --> 00:15:13,540
who can cast weird spells or have tons of mana,

240
00:15:13,700 --> 00:15:15,780
but aren't associated with the Magician's Guild yet.

241
00:15:16,080 --> 00:15:19,300
Then if they get famous later, that's good publicity for the school.

242
00:15:21,180 --> 00:15:22,740
Okay, I guess that tracks.

243
00:15:23,160 --> 00:15:24,480
I do cast weird spells.

244
00:15:25,160 --> 00:15:28,360
And if they do this a lot, then it's probably not a total scam.

245
00:15:29,380 --> 00:15:32,960
Wait, so you're telling me you've never been to school, Quagmire?

246
00:15:33,500 --> 00:15:34,920
I had a private tutor.

247
00:15:35,360 --> 00:15:35,840
Wow.

248
00:15:35,840 --> 00:15:37,860
Your family must have been well off, then.

249
00:15:38,460 --> 00:15:39,180
Sort of.

250
00:15:39,560 --> 00:15:41,700
We have ties to Asura and High Nobility.

251
00:15:42,660 --> 00:15:43,220
Right.

252
00:15:43,560 --> 00:15:45,440
Sorry, remind me of your last name again?

253
00:15:45,980 --> 00:15:48,080
Greyrat of the Notos Greyrats.

254
00:15:48,420 --> 00:15:48,720
Oh.

255
00:15:50,060 --> 00:15:50,900
Greyrat, huh?

256
00:15:51,340 --> 00:15:52,860
The liege lords of Asura?

257
00:15:52,860 --> 00:15:56,580
What are you doing as a solo adventurer way out here, then?

258
00:15:58,680 --> 00:15:59,680
Well, my folks...

259
00:16:01,360 --> 00:16:02,680
Oh, uh...

260
00:16:02,680 --> 00:16:03,720
I shouldn't have asked.

261
00:16:03,980 --> 00:16:06,620
But they went out of their way to offer you a pretty good deal.

262
00:16:06,920 --> 00:16:09,460
You might as well go down there and hear them out at least.

263
00:16:09,900 --> 00:16:10,340
You know?

264
00:16:10,340 --> 00:16:11,100
Yeah.

265
00:16:11,920 --> 00:16:17,860
And come to think of it, the only reason I went to Tudor Eris in the first place was so I could save up tuition money.

266
00:16:18,800 --> 00:16:20,020
I'd totally forgotten.

267
00:16:20,860 --> 00:16:23,740
Attending the university with Sylphie was the original goal.

268
00:16:23,740 --> 00:16:27,480
I wonder what she's been up to all this time.

269
00:16:28,620 --> 00:16:29,860
I hope she's alright.

270
00:16:31,660 --> 00:16:33,120
You should listen to him.

271
00:16:33,580 --> 00:16:35,100
School is a wonderful option.

272
00:16:35,420 --> 00:16:38,480
Especially when the only alternative would be rejoining Paul.

273
00:16:39,020 --> 00:16:39,560
You think?

274
00:16:39,560 --> 00:16:42,660
I feel like reuniting my family ought to come first.

275
00:16:43,360 --> 00:16:46,240
Paul is eventually going to bring them all back to Asura anyway.

276
00:16:46,780 --> 00:16:51,440
Just wait till they make it back safely and get settled in and then take a shorter trip to visit them.

277
00:16:51,960 --> 00:16:55,500
You're saying that because you don't want to see my father again, aren't you?

278
00:16:56,160 --> 00:16:57,380
Guilty as charged.

279
00:16:58,280 --> 00:17:00,140
Whoa, she must really hate him.

280
00:17:01,200 --> 00:17:03,360
Well, improving my skills is important.

281
00:17:03,360 --> 00:17:10,100
But attractive as the university's proposal is, I don't think I can justify taking them up on it right now.

282
00:17:24,420 --> 00:17:25,960
Long time no see.

283
00:17:26,740 --> 00:17:27,680
Yep, hi.

284
00:17:28,140 --> 00:17:29,740
What has it been, two years now?

285
00:17:30,040 --> 00:17:32,500
I don't feel as nasty as I did before.

286
00:17:33,240 --> 00:17:34,860
Aw, you missed me, huh?

287
00:17:35,700 --> 00:17:36,980
That's not what I said.

288
00:17:38,000 --> 00:17:42,780
Although, hey, I did try to reach out to you a bunch of times while I was out looking for Zenith.

289
00:17:43,240 --> 00:17:45,500
Would it have killed you to show up for me even once?

290
00:17:45,820 --> 00:17:47,860
I had a lot going on on my end.

291
00:17:48,460 --> 00:17:49,220
Aw, yeah.

292
00:17:49,980 --> 00:17:52,060
Well, at least someone eventually found her.

293
00:17:52,620 --> 00:17:54,780
Just feels like I lost two whole years over it.

294
00:17:55,340 --> 00:17:56,180
Yeah, sorry.

295
00:17:56,420 --> 00:17:58,060
But I'm glad you know where she is.

296
00:17:58,420 --> 00:17:58,800
Thanks.

297
00:17:58,800 --> 00:18:01,720
I had no idea Roxy was out there looking for her, too.

298
00:18:02,500 --> 00:18:04,700
She's a real go-getter, isn't she?

299
00:18:05,380 --> 00:18:06,640
Yeah, you said it.

300
00:18:06,740 --> 00:18:09,960
But I hope she gets back from Beggarite sooner than later.

301
00:18:10,080 --> 00:18:11,300
I can't wait to see her.

302
00:18:12,000 --> 00:18:12,600
Oh, dear.

303
00:18:13,440 --> 00:18:16,440
Are you sure you want your master to see how pathetic you are right now?

304
00:18:17,280 --> 00:18:17,680
Hey.

305
00:18:17,680 --> 00:18:19,360
I mean, think about it.

306
00:18:19,500 --> 00:18:20,680
Aeris ran out on you.

307
00:18:20,840 --> 00:18:24,980
And when you finally had a good thing going with Sarah, your little guy just wouldn't go to bat for you.

308
00:18:25,520 --> 00:18:29,820
Your spellcasting may have improved a little, but you're really hitting a wall lately.

309
00:18:29,980 --> 00:18:32,340
And your swordsmanship hasn't gotten any better either.

310
00:18:32,560 --> 00:18:36,260
I know you practice every day, but boy, you don't have much to show for it.

311
00:18:36,260 --> 00:18:42,720
Sure, you've built some muscle, but I don't think you can stand before her and say with any confidence that you're a student to be proud of, Rudy.

312
00:18:43,340 --> 00:18:45,600
Wow, you're really letting me have it this time, huh?

313
00:18:45,820 --> 00:18:47,360
How about you get to the point already?

314
00:18:48,700 --> 00:18:51,740
The point is that you have a chance to shape up!

315
00:18:52,420 --> 00:18:54,880
Attend the university, and I can promise you this.

316
00:18:54,940 --> 00:18:58,660
You'll learn so much more than a common adventurer could ever hope to.

317
00:18:59,660 --> 00:19:00,620
What are you?

318
00:19:00,740 --> 00:19:02,540
Every teacher I had in high school?

319
00:19:03,000 --> 00:19:03,500
Oh, wait.

320
00:19:03,780 --> 00:19:07,860
You just kind of threw that out there, but is that more of your patented godly advice?

321
00:19:08,100 --> 00:19:09,660
Sure, you could say that.

322
00:19:10,200 --> 00:19:14,080
You do this thing where literally everything you say sounds suspicious and creepy.

323
00:19:14,560 --> 00:19:14,960
Sorry!

324
00:19:15,380 --> 00:19:17,020
But you really should listen this time.

325
00:19:17,100 --> 00:19:18,860
I'm giving it to you as straight as I can.

326
00:19:18,860 --> 00:19:22,960
If you set out for Beggarite now, you will most assuredly regret it.

327
00:19:23,980 --> 00:19:25,360
Really? Why?

328
00:19:26,000 --> 00:19:26,880
Can't tell you.

329
00:19:27,400 --> 00:19:28,500
Of course you can't.

330
00:19:28,740 --> 00:19:31,200
Well, this isn't the first time you've kept something important from me,

331
00:19:31,280 --> 00:19:34,700
but you've got to realize that this whole interdimensional man of mystery thing

332
00:19:34,700 --> 00:19:38,260
doesn't exactly make a strong argument for whatever you're trying to get me to do.

333
00:19:38,720 --> 00:19:42,820
I'd love to take time for myself, but I'd much rather find the rest of my family first.

334
00:19:43,140 --> 00:19:43,640
I see.

335
00:19:44,220 --> 00:19:46,320
Well, why don't I put it to you another way?

336
00:19:46,680 --> 00:19:47,840
This ought to be good.

337
00:19:48,860 --> 00:19:54,060
Rudeus, enroll in the Rinoa University of Magic

338
00:19:54,060 --> 00:19:58,340
and investigate the displacement incident with their abundant resources.

339
00:19:59,680 --> 00:20:04,520
If you do, you shall once again regain your manly potency

340
00:20:04,520 --> 00:20:06,580
and, more importantly, your pride!

341
00:20:07,160 --> 00:20:08,080
Huh? Really?

342
00:20:08,440 --> 00:20:12,300
Are you saying that just by going to school, I can cure my erectile dysfunction?

343
00:20:12,640 --> 00:20:14,060
You are right!

344
00:20:14,060 --> 00:20:36,180
Sure enough, not a peep from the peen.

345
00:20:36,180 --> 00:20:48,980
Well, okay.

346
00:20:49,880 --> 00:20:50,920
Guess it'll get better.

347
00:20:50,920 --> 00:21:06,440
Thank you for everything.

348
00:21:07,240 --> 00:21:07,960
Good luck, kid.

349
00:21:08,380 --> 00:21:09,540
Take care of yourself.

350
00:21:09,540 --> 00:21:15,960
Sol, I really appreciate you.

351
00:21:16,600 --> 00:21:17,040
Huh?

352
00:21:17,460 --> 00:21:21,340
I don't know how I can ever repay all the things that you and your party have done for me.

353
00:21:22,460 --> 00:21:26,960
He may not want to admit it, but he's taken really good care of me these past couple of years.

354
00:21:26,960 --> 00:21:32,520
In fact, I've made pretty nice money exploiting your ass, so thanks for that.

355
00:21:33,820 --> 00:21:35,460
Anyway, safe travels.

356
00:21:36,100 --> 00:21:36,920
Go get cured.

357
00:21:37,780 --> 00:21:39,200
Yeah, I'll try.

358
00:21:39,720 --> 00:21:40,020
Good.

359
00:21:40,020 --> 00:21:44,060
Well, I'm sure we'll have business over in Rinoa one of these days.

360
00:21:44,460 --> 00:21:49,080
And when that happens, we ought to go drinking and whoring again, just the two of us.

361
00:21:57,480 --> 00:22:01,080
And so, I set out for the kingdom of Rinoa.

362
00:22:01,080 --> 00:22:31,060
And so, I'm going to go to the kingdom of Rinoa.

363
00:23:35,890 --> 00:23:38,650
Laya, Laya

